LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Kung makakapag-mabili.

1182
01:05:31,480 --> 01:05:36,840
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Ang balak po namin doon is gamitin yung mga water bladders na ibibigay ng TENR.

1183
01:05:37,600 --> 01:05:46,940
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Pupunuin na po namin ng tubig yun at i-replace namin sa mga water districts na na-identify namin na talagang magiging stressful ang kanilang sitwasyon.

1184
01:05:47,620 --> 01:05:51,620
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Gagamitin rin namin yan to fill water lorries for deployment.

1185
01:05:52,100 --> 01:05:54,000
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Pwede kasi silang patakboy ng 24 hours.

1186
01:05:54,160 --> 01:05:58,280
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Tapos magpupunun lang tayo ng mga tanket bladders.

1187
01:05:58,840 --> 01:06:01,860
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Ilang water bladders na ang nasa kamay ng department?

1188
01:06:03,480 --> 01:06:07,000
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Madam Chair, parang ano yata? 13 or 15?

1189
01:06:09,560 --> 01:06:12,780
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: 30. 30 pala. Sorry Madam Chair. 30.

1190
01:06:13,160 --> 01:06:17,740
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: 1-3 Madam Chair. 1-3. 13.

1191
01:06:18,020 --> 01:06:19,940
Senator Risa Hontiveros: 13 lamang. Oo, Secretary.

1192
01:06:21,760 --> 01:06:23,360
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And sapat na po ba yun?

1193
01:06:23,520 --> 01:06:28,820
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Or balak din ang department na mag-procure whether by the end of the year or sa bago?

1194
01:06:28,940 --> 01:06:30,020
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Noong taong 2027.

1195
01:06:31,960 --> 01:06:36,880
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: If we have the funding Madam Chair, we can add to this.

1196
01:06:36,880 --> 01:06:45,580
Senator Risa Hontiveros: From 13, ilan ang optimal at efficient number na dapat merong ang department?

1197
01:06:50,560 --> 01:06:52,200
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Sir Secretary, Madam Chair.

1198
01:06:53,820 --> 01:06:55,700
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Ma'am, if I may suggest.

1199
01:06:55,720 --> 01:06:56,740
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Yes, Admin Salonga.

1200
01:06:56,920 --> 01:06:57,900
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Kahit 50.

1201
01:06:58,840 --> 01:07:08,440
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: 50 po. Para we can replace them immediately in large water districts for deployment in areas na talagang wala.

1202
01:07:08,820 --> 01:07:13,100
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Nandiyan na ba yan sa proposed budget ng department sa line item na yun?

1203
01:07:13,560 --> 01:07:14,460
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Sa luwa po.

1204
01:07:14,660 --> 01:07:15,380
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Sa luwa?

1205
01:07:15,520 --> 01:07:17,420
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Opo. Bibigay na lang po namin sa inyo.

1206
01:07:17,720 --> 01:07:19,380
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Okay. So wala pa dun sa ngayon?

1207
01:07:19,760 --> 01:07:25,320
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Okay. So this is times 4 ng current na meron na 13.

1208
01:07:25,960 --> 01:07:26,400
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Okay.

1209
01:07:28,840 --> 01:07:31,380
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Then, syempre, nasa ilalim nyo yung mga water districts.

1210
01:07:31,520 --> 01:07:36,560
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Paano nyo ipopromote yung collaboration sa pagitan ng mga water districts?

1211
01:07:36,560 --> 01:07:39,340
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Lalo na yung mga adjacent, yung mga magkakatabi.

1212
01:07:40,060 --> 01:07:47,160
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Limbawa, may sapat na tubig yung isang water district pero nagkukulang naman yung katabing lugar, yung adjacent na lugar.

1213
01:07:47,980 --> 01:07:52,420
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Paano nyo sila matutulungan magbahagi ng supply sa isa't isa?

1214
01:07:52,900 --> 01:07:57,440
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Madam Chair, Mr. Secretary, actually yun po maganda dun sa water district regime natin.

1215
01:07:57,720 --> 01:07:58,360
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Talagang.

1216
01:07:58,840 --> 01:08:05,160
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: In the 53 years ng luwa, nagkaroon sila ng parang coordination amongst their clustered water districts.

1217
01:08:05,160 --> 01:08:06,940
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: So talagang nagtutulungan sila.

1218
01:08:07,060 --> 01:08:17,120
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Even in events of travesty or merong sakuna dun, ang unang response ng water district is from the neighboring water district.

1219
01:08:17,660 --> 01:08:23,640
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Bago before big government moves in, yung mga magkakatabing water districts ang nagtutulungan.

1220
01:08:24,040 --> 01:08:25,720
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: So we can actually pre-place them.

1221
01:08:25,880 --> 01:08:28,560
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Saka hindi naman ako nababahala na hindi sila magtutulungan.

1222
01:08:28,840 --> 01:08:30,840
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Talagang nagtutulungan po sila.

1223
01:08:33,600 --> 01:08:40,340
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So walang kailangan kayong ipromote? May reflex na, may natural behavior na sila?

1224
01:08:40,760 --> 01:08:47,200
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Or meron pa ba kayong idadagdag na pako-ordination sa kanila sa harap ng Super El Nino?

1225
01:08:47,500 --> 01:08:51,320
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Madam Chair, nandun na po sa memorandum circular po yun. Tapos clustered po sila.

1226
01:08:51,700 --> 01:08:54,660
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Meron rin sila mga regional organization ng water districts.

1227
01:08:55,000 --> 01:08:58,660
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: So madali silang makapag-move, communicate, and help each other.

1228
01:08:58,840 --> 01:08:59,900
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Other in times of tragedy.

1229
01:09:00,900 --> 01:09:09,920
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Balik na rin naman natin, paano nyo i-handle kung magkaroon ng conflict o kaya disputes sa pagitan nitong mga water districts?

1230
01:09:10,400 --> 01:09:11,360
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Pati LGUs, no?

1231
01:09:11,880 --> 01:09:19,140
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Yung mga nag-host ng water sources at yung mga LGU na purely consumer lang ng tubig.

1232
01:09:19,320 --> 01:09:28,180
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Parang writ small yung sinasabing tension lagi sa, kunyari, mga regyon sa mundo tulad ng Middle East na tubig talaga ang pinakamahalaga

1233
01:09:28,180 --> 01:09:29,860
Senator Risa Hontiveros: at maaring pag-awayang resource.

1234
01:09:30,020 --> 01:09:35,920
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Madam Chair, nakikita namin yan. Pero yung water allocation is actually not a distribution issue.

1235
01:09:36,300 --> 01:09:39,340
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: It's more of an allocation dito galing po sa NWRB.

1236
01:09:39,720 --> 01:09:48,260
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: But nakikita na namin yan ngayon kasi for example, there are some metro water districts that take water from other cities

1237
01:09:48,260 --> 01:09:54,100
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: and yung local city that hosts the water source want to de-annex to preserve their own water source.

1238
01:09:54,100 --> 01:09:56,820
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: So meron na pong conflicts na ganyan nangyayari.

1239
01:09:56,820 --> 01:10:09,020
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Kasi sinusubukan na lang naming ayusin by ensuring that the host water, the host LGU that has the water is first satisfied doon sa demands nila.

1240
01:10:09,520 --> 01:10:14,540
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: At that level, kaya ng luwa. Pero yung allocation po mismo ng water source, hindi po sa amin doon.

1241
01:10:15,540 --> 01:10:20,580
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Baka sometimes during this hearing, gustong mag-weigh in ang NWRB tungkol dito.

1242
01:10:23,780 --> 01:10:25,940
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Paano pinipreempt or nire-resolve?

1243
01:10:25,940 --> 01:10:30,180
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Kapag nga magkaroon ng ganitong conflict or disputes.

1244
01:10:30,280 --> 01:10:32,900
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Would you like to input something at this point, Dr. David?

1245
01:10:33,240 --> 01:10:37,200
NWRB Executive Director Sevillo D. David Jr.: Yes, ma'am. Good afternoon, Madam Chair. With the permission of the Secretary.

1246
01:10:38,000 --> 01:10:47,580
NWRB Executive Director Sevillo D. David Jr.: Yes, Madam Chair. In terms of allocation and water rights, ang NWRB po is with the authority and quasi-judicial function

1247
01:10:47,580 --> 01:10:51,700
NWRB Executive Director Sevillo D. David Jr.: to resolve po yung mga conflicts between bar use, water use.

1248
01:10:51,700 --> 01:10:55,020
NWRB Executive Director Sevillo D. David Jr.: But of course, as per water code po, Madam Chair,

1249
01:10:55,940 --> 01:11:04,940
NWRB Executive Director Sevillo D. David Jr.: priority po yung domestic and household use in the evaluation and assessment of water use or water rights.

1250
01:11:05,160 --> 01:11:16,520
NWRB Executive Director Sevillo D. David Jr.: At of course, tinitingnan po natin din dyan yung availability ng tubig po for a certain area kung saan po nagkakaroon ng conflict.

1251
01:11:16,520 --> 01:11:25,920
NWRB Executive Director Sevillo D. David Jr.: But of course, with the condition that must priority po yung domestic and household use over irrigation and of course power and other.

1252
01:11:25,940 --> 01:11:38,340
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Sa ngayon po, Dr. David, may bilang na ba kayo ng mga magkakatabi or adjacent na water districts na mayroon or magkakaroon ng ganitong dispute o conflict?

1253
01:11:38,480 --> 01:11:45,000
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So between isang water-resourced at yung isang water-dependent na water district or LGU?

1254
01:11:45,660 --> 01:11:51,740
NWRB Executive Director Sevillo D. David Jr.: Yes po, Madam Chair. Meron po kaming mga listing ng potential conflict.

1255
01:11:51,740 --> 01:11:55,280
NWRB Executive Director Sevillo D. David Jr.: But usually po, di naman between water district.

1256
01:11:55,940 --> 01:12:01,720
NWRB Executive Director Sevillo D. David Jr.: Actually po, between water district and the local government unit or some water service providers po.

1257
01:12:02,660 --> 01:12:07,160
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Mga ilan yung ganitong dispute or conflict areas all over the country?

1258
01:12:08,020 --> 01:12:13,160
NWRB Executive Director Sevillo D. David Jr.: If with the provision of the Chair, pwede po namin i-provide yung list later on.

1259
01:12:13,620 --> 01:12:16,700
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Please do. Either during this hearing or bago nung plenary.

1260
01:12:16,700 --> 01:12:25,460
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And in general, kung ilan man ang mga ito na may actual or potential conflict, may sapat na panahon ba?

1261
01:12:25,460 --> 01:12:31,640
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Ang NWRB para i-resolve ito bago tumama yung pinakamalakas na epekto ng Super El Nino?

1262
01:12:32,040 --> 01:12:37,540
NWRB Executive Director Sevillo D. David Jr.: Ang strategy po na Madam Chair ngayon is to resolve yung mga conflict kung saan po yung mga water stress.

1263
01:12:37,640 --> 01:12:40,760
NWRB Executive Director Sevillo D. David Jr.: You prioritize po kung saan po yung mga water stress areas.

1264
01:12:41,900 --> 01:12:50,780
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Priority nyo. Pero hindi ko matansya yung scale kasi bibigay nyo pa lang sa subcommittee namin yung bilang.

1265
01:12:50,780 --> 01:12:55,120
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Pero kakayanin nyo po ba ma-resolve itong mga priority?

1266
01:12:55,460 --> 01:13:01,220
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Conflict or dispute areas bago pa nga yung kasagsagan ng Super El Nino?

1267
01:13:02,180 --> 01:13:06,200
NWRB Executive Director Sevillo D. David Jr.: We will tingnan po muna namin yung timeline, Madam Chair.

1268
01:13:09,760 --> 01:13:13,720
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Sige po. Pahingin na lang nung data na yun para matignan din yung subcommittee namin.

1269
01:13:14,460 --> 01:13:22,340
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And then, last sa paksang ito, nakausap nyo na po ba ang DPWH?

1270
01:13:23,180 --> 01:13:24,980
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Whether NWRB or LUA?

1271
01:13:25,460 --> 01:13:34,140
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Usap ba ang DP ukol sa pagtap ng pondo para sa level 1 water supply system since yan po ang hawak ng DP?

1272
01:13:34,920 --> 01:13:36,420
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Yes, Administrator Salonga.

1273
01:13:36,560 --> 01:13:39,680
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Madam Chair, Mr. Secretary, bukas po may meeting po kami.

1274
01:13:40,900 --> 01:13:43,700
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Makipag-meeting po ako kay Sec. Dizon regarding that matter.

1275
01:13:45,080 --> 01:13:46,260
Senator Risa Hontiveros: When are you meeting the Secretary?

1276
01:13:46,560 --> 01:13:47,060
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Tomorrow po.

1277
01:13:47,060 --> 01:13:50,020
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Sorry, tomorrow. Okay, great. So well within the budget season.

1278
01:13:50,480 --> 01:13:53,660
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Paki-update na lang yung subcommittee namin tungkol dyan.

1279
01:13:55,460 --> 01:14:04,320
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Before we move on to the MWSSRO, just a few follow-up questions.

1280
01:14:04,760 --> 01:14:06,320
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Ayan, bago lang magpatuloy.

1281
01:14:06,860 --> 01:14:13,220
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Tanong kay Sec. Kuna, ipipresent nyo po ba yung budget ng OSEC and attached agencies?

1282
01:14:17,000 --> 01:14:22,120
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Para yung mga slides makita at mapag-usapan natin.

1283
01:14:22,420 --> 01:14:22,820
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Oo.

1284
01:14:24,340 --> 01:14:25,440
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Madam Chair, we just.

1285
01:14:25,460 --> 01:14:28,980
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Yes, please. Thank you. So you'll be able to do that during this hearing?

1286
01:14:29,140 --> 01:14:38,520
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Okay, better. Kasi ganun din kami sanay na may pace at saka may supporting visuals.

1287
01:14:38,780 --> 01:14:42,640
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Madam Chair, if I may add, still on the same topic on El Nino.

1288
01:14:43,400 --> 01:14:52,480
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: We have, through an executive order in 2023 from the President, the Water Resource Management Office was created.

1289
01:14:52,480 --> 01:15:00,100
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Supposedly, it was a precursor for the Department of Water, Madam Chair.

1290
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:13,380
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: So this is under the DENR, which is why we have integrated the other water-related offices under this WRMO, namely NWRB.

1291
01:15:00,120 --> 01:15:01,400
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: ...

1292
01:15:13,540 --> 01:15:22,800
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Well, NWRB has been our attached agency since time immemorial, but the LUA and the MWSS, kasama na rin po namin.

1293
01:15:22,800 --> 01:15:30,320
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: But under the WRMO itself, they have some proposed projects also for next year.

1294
01:15:30,520 --> 01:15:34,960
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: But actually, they're existing projects and there are some projects proposed for next year.

1295
01:15:35,040 --> 01:15:39,800
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: These are specifically water filtration program, desalination.

1296
01:15:40,860 --> 01:15:46,340
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: These are small infrastructure, small structures, Madam Chair.

1297
01:15:46,340 --> 01:15:52,120
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Water filtration for fresh water and then refilling stations, water tanks.

1298
01:15:52,120 --> 01:15:54,120
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: For water districts or LGUs.

1299
01:15:54,260 --> 01:16:02,320
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: And then yung geo-resistivity survey, Madam Chair, which is essentially like exploration for more water resources.

1300
01:16:03,360 --> 01:16:05,700
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: So there's a budget proposed for this.

1301
01:16:05,840 --> 01:16:12,320
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: It's 223,064,000 total for these different.

1302
01:16:12,420 --> 01:16:17,920
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: There are existing projects already, Madam Chair, which I have actually personally visited a few of them.

1303
01:16:17,920 --> 01:16:20,920
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: And they're very beneficial.

1304
01:16:20,920 --> 01:16:35,720
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Beneficial in the sense that most of these identified areas we chose were those which were very hard to reach or underserved talaga in terms of access to water, Madam Chair.

1305
01:16:36,860 --> 01:16:43,800
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And SEC, itong 223,000,000 para sa lahat ng klase ng mga small water impounding systems na ito.

1306
01:16:43,880 --> 01:16:46,020
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Kasama na po ba ito dun sa...

1307
01:16:46,020 --> 01:16:46,760
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Madam Chair, if I may.

1308
01:16:46,880 --> 01:16:47,920
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Hindi ko mga...

1309
01:16:48,460 --> 01:16:49,020
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Hindi ko mga Swiss ito.

1310
01:16:49,080 --> 01:16:49,560
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Sorry.

1311
01:16:49,560 --> 01:16:50,560
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Water filtration program.

1312
01:16:50,920 --> 01:16:51,800
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Programs yung iba.

1313
01:16:53,060 --> 01:16:54,320
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Summer desalination.

1314
01:16:54,480 --> 01:16:55,280
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Yung iba, fresh water.

1315
01:16:55,420 --> 01:16:57,560
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Para lang maging potable to the people.

1316
01:16:57,960 --> 01:16:58,600
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: The access lang.

1317
01:16:58,700 --> 01:17:10,120
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Because many of these are in island communities, island barangays, or really far-flung areas that people have to travel very far to get access to water.

1318
01:17:10,120 --> 01:17:16,460
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: So there are certain areas that we pinpointed that we put up these projects, Madam Chair.

1319
01:17:19,560 --> 01:17:20,340
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Salamat, SEC.

1320
01:17:20,920 --> 01:17:32,440
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So before we go on to the MWRO, a question actually na nabanggit din kanina about, I think it was the Secretary, about Manila Water, Maynilad, for example.

1321
01:17:34,440 --> 01:17:43,240
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Paalala lang, SEC or USEC Annalisa, to please prepare the data for the subcommittee on the most vulnerable areas.

1322
01:17:43,760 --> 01:17:47,100
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Most, middling, and least vulnerable to Super El Nino.

1323
01:17:47,920 --> 01:17:50,760
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And kung handa na rin kayo at that point with the...

1324
01:17:50,760 --> 01:17:57,860
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Overlay map para ma-read into the record yung mga areas most vulnerable dun sa Super El Nino.

1325
01:17:58,440 --> 01:18:01,740
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Are you ready already now, USEC Annalisa, or shall, in a bit?

1326
01:18:04,640 --> 01:18:09,800
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Our technical person is not here to show the overlay of the map, but...

1327
01:18:09,800 --> 01:18:12,560
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Babalik ba siya? Darating ba siya later in the hearing?

1328
01:18:13,280 --> 01:18:16,120
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Usually, pag-budget hearing, the technical people are here.

1329
01:18:16,920 --> 01:18:17,820
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Bakit wala?

1330
01:18:18,220 --> 01:18:20,640
Senator Risa Hontiveros: We did that into the mapping.

1331
01:18:20,760 --> 01:18:28,100
Senator Risa Hontiveros: We need the data on the most vulnerable areas, and pag-visual, mas nakakatulong, pati sa subcommittee.

1332
01:18:29,720 --> 01:18:31,740
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, that can be read into the record.

1333
01:18:32,380 --> 01:18:34,040
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Sige, ma'am, we'll wait for that during this hearing.

1334
01:18:34,160 --> 01:18:37,880
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, let's go on to questions to the MWRO.

1335
01:18:40,280 --> 01:18:40,960
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Sino po?

1336
01:18:43,800 --> 01:18:44,980
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Chief Regulator T.

1337
01:18:45,260 --> 01:18:45,500
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Yes.

1338
01:18:45,500 --> 01:18:45,980
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Okay, sir.

1339
01:18:47,240 --> 01:18:50,600
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, moving from DNR...

1340
01:18:50,760 --> 01:18:58,540
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Ano naman naghahanda para sa Super El Nino, yung mga malalaking water concessionaires ng MWSS, so, Maynilad and Manila Water?

