Senator Risa Hontiveros: Yes.

1705
01:39:11,400 --> 01:39:17,240
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Great. Tamang-tama. Before going on to other concerns with these agencies, please, let's backtrack to that.

1706
01:39:17,240 --> 01:39:25,700
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Yung map overlay na ginawa nyo para identify yung three levels of vulnerability and projected

1707
01:39:25,740 --> 01:39:29,200
Senator Risa Hontiveros: impact by the Super El Ni?o,

1708
01:39:29,220 --> 01:39:30,940
Senator Risa Hontiveros: please proceed Yusek, Analisa.

1709
01:39:31,040 --> 01:39:35,800
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: Madam Chair, ma'am, may I introduce Ms. Villa Estolero to present the map?

1710
01:39:37,720 --> 01:39:43,020
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Parang presiding officer namin on your mind. Parang I read Estolero. Estolero ba? Escudero?

1711
01:39:43,800 --> 01:39:45,620
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: Estolero po, Madam Chair.

1712
01:39:45,780 --> 01:39:48,020
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Okay. So, please proceed, Ms. Villa.

1713
01:39:49,100 --> 01:39:49,900
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: Ay, ma'am.

1714
01:39:55,740 --> 01:40:25,720
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: Thank you.

1715
01:40:25,720 --> 01:40:38,140
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: While the map is waiting to be flashed, I will explain the methodology of how the most vulnerable barangays were assessed based on available spatial data.

1716
01:40:38,140 --> 01:40:54,560
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: So first of all, we have three available data when we weighted criteria po ng mga most vulnerable sa drought.

1717
01:40:54,560 --> 01:41:08,740
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: We have the DOST Pag-asa Drought Projections by December 2026 and the Groundwater Stressed Areas from NWRB based on their latest available data of 2025.

1718
01:41:09,600 --> 01:41:22,460
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: And the Water Service Provider Data based on NWRB Listahang Tubig 2025, DILG Subay Bayan, and available WRMO data.

1719
01:41:22,460 --> 01:41:25,760
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: So these three factors were weighted.

1720
01:41:26,500 --> 01:41:32,880
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: So for groundwater stress, there's a score of 1 for groundwater stress and 0 for non-groundwater.

1721
01:41:33,300 --> 01:41:43,400
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: Water service coverage, 1 if there are no water service providers in the area and 0 if it is covered by a water service provider.

1722
01:41:43,400 --> 01:41:49,180
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: And the Pag-asa Drought Outlook based on the classification of DOST Pag-asa.

1723
01:41:49,500 --> 01:41:52,040
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: Drought for 3, dry spell for 2.

1724
01:41:52,460 --> 01:41:54,720
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: Dry condition 1, then not affected 0.

1725
01:41:55,400 --> 01:41:58,340
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: Then the scores were summed to determine the priority category.

1726
01:41:58,340 --> 01:42:01,760
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: So high priority with a total score of greater than 3.

1727
01:42:02,360 --> 01:42:05,760
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: Moderate priority with a total score of equal to 2.

1728
01:42:06,160 --> 01:42:08,340
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: Low priority with a total score of equal to 1.

1729
01:42:08,620 --> 01:42:10,600
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: And not affected with a total score of 0.

1730
01:42:11,260 --> 01:42:16,980
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: So based on the spatial assessment and GIS analysis of the Geospatial Database Office,

1731
01:42:17,620 --> 01:42:21,720
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: we have come up that there are 14,434 barangays.

1732
01:42:22,460 --> 01:42:26,500
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: Or 34% of the barangays nationwide, which are deemed high priority.

1733
01:42:27,040 --> 01:42:32,980
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: But do note that this assessment is indicative only and based on available spatial data.

1734
01:42:33,540 --> 01:42:34,560
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: And that's how we come up.

1735
01:42:34,780 --> 01:42:39,460
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: And for moderate priority, 17,046 barangays, 41%.

1736
01:42:40,300 --> 01:42:43,460
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: Low priority, 9,685, 23%.

1737
01:42:44,020 --> 01:42:48,460
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: And not affected, or 883 barangays, or 2%.

1738
01:42:48,460 --> 01:42:50,460
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: But there is a specific...

1739
01:42:52,460 --> 01:42:58,800
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: Disclaimer that this is based on the drought data of Pag-Asa forecast for December 2026.

1740
01:43:00,340 --> 01:43:02,480
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Thank you so much, Ms. Via.

1741
01:43:02,940 --> 01:43:08,660
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So itong pag-identify niyo unang-una ng 14,000 high priority barangays,

1742
01:43:08,740 --> 01:43:11,420
Senator Risa Hontiveros: or 34% ng mga barangays sa ating bansa.

1743
01:43:12,140 --> 01:43:16,040
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So naka-align na po ba sa mga ito,

1744
01:43:16,040 --> 01:43:22,380
Senator Risa Hontiveros: yung mga Super El Nino preparation and response programs,

1745
01:43:22,460 --> 01:43:26,200
Senator Risa Hontiveros: activities and projects ng department in the budget so far?

1746
01:43:30,340 --> 01:43:34,540
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: For Madam Chair, for that information, we would have to confirm.

1747
01:43:35,000 --> 01:43:41,220
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: But for the available data, we have several projects for WRMO,

1748
01:43:41,220 --> 01:43:51,740
